J. Maurice Rojas
Mathematics
Professor

J. Maurice Rojas received his Ph.D. from the University of California at 
Berkeley in 1995 and joined the Mathematics Department in 2001 after 
postdoctoral positions at MSRI, MIT, and City University of Hong Kong.  
Tenured and promoted in 2003, he later held visiting positions at 
Johns Hopkins University, IMA, and Sandia National Laboratories.  His 
research --- in algebraic geometry and algorithmic complexity --- is funded 
by the NSF, including a CAREER Award.  Dr. Rojas is known as one of the best 
teachers in the department as well as a great mentor for graduate and 
undergraduate students. He has published extensively, organized international 
workshops and conferences, was a summer Research Experiences for Undergraduates 
(REU) mentor 4 times, and was a member of the department.s executive committee 
and the university's Homeland Security Initiative.

